  "review_findings": [
    "Finalization performs source debt inspection inside the existing BEGIN IMMEDIATE owner-fenced transaction. New deliveries and source failure cannot publish worker.result before that boundary is discharged.",
    "The source-failure draft, blocked Worker/run/node state, lease clearing, and worker.blocked event are written in one transaction. The earlier manual commit and second _fail transaction were removed.",
    "Debt is based on actual same-run delivery records. Even an unread delivery must pass existing scope, event/inbox, source hash and revocation validation. A consumed preview alone cannot discharge debt.",
    "Checkpoint framing distinguishes Core delivery of untrusted Thread context from its payload's authority, while retaining the legacy wrapper for other input. The existing provenance-test fixture adds one actual full read; its original partial read and tamper assertions remain intact.",
    "Valid reads require existing Core proofs, model selection, a matching tool-result transcript before the candidate's ordinal, and complete current payload coverage; explicit Core-proved handback remains available. Unknown or failed reads do not become proofs.",
    "A refused final draft stays charged and persisted. Existing step/token/tool/output limits and unknown-call handling remain unchanged. Feedback only names remaining references and offsets, and grants no new authority."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This source repair has targeted/offline validation only. No new live condition or full backend suite was run after the user's stop/hand-off instruction.",
    "Complete context reading is an execution boundary, not a claim of understanding or typed multihop Recall. The unchanged acceptance oracle may still fail and old failed reports remain failed.",
    "The production gate allows source-matching overlapping page coverage; the existing acceptance evidence additionally requires sequential model-selected pagination. No oracle was loosened to make them agree.",
    "The returned final candidate establishes a later model-call boundary after stored tool results under the existing Worker execution loop; neither captured raw HTTP input nor model internal understanding is claimed.",
    "The f87 current packet recheck changes after a later global recap constraint. Its independent audit reconstructs original hashes with an explicit read-only historical constraint frontier; this source repair does not change that separate behavior.",
    "Old round3 full-suite results apply to their recorded source. They are not attributed to the new helper or final two changed production files."
  ]
